module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalFunctions.StalkFormalFunctionsFrom02O8
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionProper.ArtinReesChain

/-!
# Clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 02OB], on its own

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` a proper morphism, `ℱ` a
coherent sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules and `p ≥ 0`. Write `𝓘 = I · 𝒪_X`. [Stacks, Tag 02OB] produces a
single integer `c ≥ 0` serving three clauses at once; it is
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.exists_uniform_bound_cohomology_idealPowerQuotient_of_isProper`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/CompletionProper/ArtinReesChain.lean`), where the
tag is registered.

This file records its first clause,

`Ker(Hᵖ(X, ℱ) → Hᵖ(X, ℱ / 𝓘ⁿℱ)) ⊆ Iⁿ⁻ᶜ · Hᵖ(X, ℱ)` for every `n ≥ c`,

as a statement of its own, with coherence spelled `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent`, because that
is the clause the degree-zero comparison of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/CompletionProper/DirectImageAdicBound.lean`
consumes.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.ker_cohomology_idealPowerQuotient_le` — clause (1) of
  [Stacks, Tag 02OB].

## Implementation notes

The reading of `Iⁿ⁻ᶜ · Hᵖ(X, ℱ)` is the one fixed in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalFunctions/IdealPowerQuotientCohomologyBound.lean`: the
`A`-submodule generated by the products, which is why the clause is stated after restriction of
scalars along `baseRingHom`.

Coherence is spelled `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent`; it is interchangeable with the
root-level predicate by `AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.isCoherent_iff_stacksIsCoherent`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open scoped ModuleCat.Algebra

universe u

namespace Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions

open Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase Stacks.Algebraization

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {X : Scheme.{u}}
  (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) (I : Ideal A) (F : X.Modules) (p : ℕ)

/-- **Clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 02OB].** The kernel of `Hᵖ(X, ℱ) → Hᵖ(X, ℱ / 𝓘ⁿℱ)` is contained
in `Iⁿ⁻ᶜ · Hᵖ(X, ℱ)` for every `n ≥ c`, for one `c` independent of `n`.

A projection of
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.exists_uniform_bound_cohomology_idealPowerQuotient_of_isProper`,
whose `c` serves this clause and the other two at once. -/
public theorem ker_cohomology_idealPowerQuotient_le
    (hX : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProper f) (hF : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent F) :
    ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, c ≤ n →
      LinearMap.ker (cohomologyOverBaseMap A f p
          (cokernel.π (C := X.Modules)
            (idealPowerMultiple (baseIdealSheaf A I f) n F).ι)).hom ≤
        I ^ (n - c) • (⊤ : Submodule A (cohomologyOverBase A f p F)) :=
  have : F.IsCoherent := AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.isCoherent_of_stacksIsCoherent hF
  let ⟨c, hker, _, _⟩ :=
    exists_uniform_bound_cohomology_idealPowerQuotient_of_isProper A f I F hX p
  ⟨c, hker⟩

end Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions

end
